 678:   void _handleControllerChanged() {
 679:     if (mounted) {
 680:       // Drop the cached laid-out painter for blocks whose content changed so a
 681:       // stale painter is not reused on the next build. Selection-only /
 682:       // composition-only changes (empty set) do not invalidate anything.
 683:       //
 684:       // The block *extent* cache is intentionally NOT invalidated here. While a
 685:       // block's text is being edited (most acutely during IME composition such
 686:       // as pinyin input) its content mutates on every keystroke, but its height
 687:       // barely changes. Dropping the cached height mid-edit would fall back to
 688:       // the document-wide average height for one frame, repositioning every
 689:       // following block — a visible flicker of the content below the caret. The
 690:       // real (possibly unchanged) height is reconciled on the next frame by the
 691:       // measured-block widget, so leaving the stale value yields one frame of a
 692:       // near-correct height instead of one frame of a wrong average.
 693:       final dirty = widget.controller.lastChangedBlockIds;
 694:       if (dirty == null) {
 695:         _extentCache.clear();
 696:       } else if (dirty.isNotEmpty) {
 697:         for (final id in dirty) {
 698:           _layoutCache.removeBlock(id);
 699:         }
 700:       }
 701:       // Keep the platform IME candidate window anchored at the caret, and
 702:       // scroll a programmatically-moved caret back into view. Both run in a
 703:       // post-frame callback so the caret's render box reflects the latest
 704:       // selection (and any keep-alive mount) before we read its global rect.
